      "settings": {
        "custom_liquid": "<script type=\"application/ld+json\">\n{\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n  \"@graph\": [\n\t{\n  \t\"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\n  \t\"@id\": \"https://strobesnmore.com/blogs/informative/ohio-emergency-vehicle-light-laws#article\",\n  \t\"isPartOf\": {\n    \t\"@id\": \"https://strobesnmore.com/blogs/informative/ohio-emergency-vehicle-light-laws#webpage\"\n  \t},\n  \t\"mainEntityOfPage\": {\n    \t\"@id\": \"https://strobesnmore.com/blogs/informative/ohio-emergency-vehicle-light-laws#webpage\"\n  \t},\n  \t\"headline\": \"Ohio Emergency Vehicle Light Laws: Colors, Classes and the Public Safety Vehicle Decal\",\n  \t\"description\": \"ORC 4513.17 by color and class, plus the Public Safety Vehicle decal program volunteers must complete annually before running lights. Reviewed September 2026.\",\n  \t\"abstract\": \"Ohio prohibits flashing lights on motor vehicles by default under Ohio Revised Code § 4513.17(C)(1), with a defined list of exceptions covering emergency vehicles, road service and towing, waste collection, rural mail delivery, highway maintenance and farm machinery. A volunteer firefighter's personal vehicle in Ohio qualifies as a public safety vehicle under ORC § 4511.01(E)(3) only when properly identified as required by the director of public safety. Color compliance alone is not sufficient. The Ohio State Fire Marshal is the certifying agency for volunteer public safety vehicles. The process requires an Ohio State Highway Patrol safety inspection, a decal application submitted by the fire department, and annual renewal. Ohio public safety vehicle decals consist of a Maltese Cross and a date sticker placed in the lower right-hand corner of the windshield, and the vehicle function is designated VF for volunteer fire fighter, VR for volunteer rescue, or both. Ohio fire departments must be current on submittal of fire incident reports before public safety vehicle decals will be issued to their members. A 2022 amendment to ORC § 4513.17 added stationary waste collection vehicles actively collecting garbage, refuse, trash or recyclable materials on the roadside to the list of vehicles permitted to display flashing, oscillating or rotating amber lights.\",\n  \t\"speakable\": {\n    \t\"@type\": \"SpeakableSpecification\",\n    \t\"cssSelector\": [\n      \t\".key-takeaways\",\n      \t\"h1\"\n    \t]\n  \t},\n  \t\"inLanguage\": \"en-US\",\n  \t\"datePublished\": \"2026-09-08\",\n  \t\"dateModified\": \"2026-09-09\",\n  \t\"author\": {\n    \t\"@id\": \"https://strobesnmore.com/#organization\"\n  \t},\n  \t\"publisher\": {\n    \t\"@id\": \"https://strobesnmore.com/#organization\"\n  \t},\n  \t\"about\": [\n    \t{\n      \t\"@type\": \"Thing\",\n      \t\"name\": \"Ohio emergency vehicle lighting law\"\n    \t},\n    \t{\n      \t\"@type\": \"Legislation\",\n      \t\"name\": \"Ohio Rev. Code §§ 4513.17, 4511.01(E)\",\n      \t\"jurisdiction\": {\n        \t\"@type\": \"AdministrativeArea\",\n        \t\"name\": \"Ohio\"\n      \t},\n      \t\"legislationJurisdiction\": \"US-OH\"\n    \t}\n  \t],\n  \t\"citation\": [\n    \t{\n      \t\"@type\": \"CreativeWork\",\n      \t\"name\": \"Ohio Revised Code § 4513.17 (Ohio Laws)\",\n      \t\"url\": \"https://codes.ohio.gov/ohio-revised-code/section-4513.17\"\n    \t},\n    \t{\n      \t\"@type\": \"CreativeWork\",\n      \t\"name\": \"Ohio Revised Code § 4511.01, public safety vehicle definitions\",\n      \t\"url\": \"https://codes.ohio.gov/ohio-revised-code/section-4511.01\"\n    \t},\n    \t{\n      \t\"@type\": \"CreativeWork\",\n      \t\"name\": \"Ohio Division of State Fire Marshal, Public Safety Vehicle Decal Information\",\n      \t\"url\": \"https://com.ohio.gov/divisions-and-programs/state-fire-marshal/fire-prevention/fire-department-guides/public-safety-vehicle-decal-information\"\n    \t}\n  \t],\n  \t\"image\": {\n    \t\"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\n    \t\"url\": \"REPLACE_WITH_FEATURED_IMAGE_URL\",\n    \t\"width\": 1200,\n    \t\"height\": 630\n  \t}\n\t},\n\t{\n  \t\"@type\": \"WebPage\",\n  \t\"@id\": \"https://strobesnmore.com/blogs/informative/ohio-emergency-vehicle-light-laws#webpage\",\n  \t\"url\": \"https://strobesnmore.com/blogs/informative/ohio-emergency-vehicle-light-laws\",\n  \t\"name\": \"Ohio Emergency Vehicle Light Laws (2026 Guide)\",\n  \t\"description\": \"ORC 4513.17 by color and class, plus the Public Safety Vehicle decal program volunteers must complete annually before running lights. Reviewed September 2026.\",\n  \t\"isPartOf\": {\n    \t\"@id\": \"https://strobesnmore.com/#website\"\n  \t},\n  \t\"breadcrumb\": {\n    \t\"@id\": \"https://strobesnmore.com/blogs/informative/ohio-emergency-vehicle-light-laws#breadcrumb\"\n  \t},\n  \t\"lastReviewed\": \"2026-09-08\",\n  \t\"reviewedBy\": {\n    \t\"@id\": \"https://strobesnmore.com/#organization\"\n  \t},\n  \t\"inLanguage\": \"en-US\"\n\t},\n\t{\n  \t\"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\",\n  \t\"@id\": \"https://strobesnmore.com/blogs/informative/ohio-emergency-vehicle-light-laws#breadcrumb\",\n  \t\"itemListElement\": [\n    \t{\n      \t\"@type\": \"ListItem\",\n      \t\"position\": 1,\n      \t\"name\": \"Home\",\n      \t\"item\": \"https://strobesnmore.com/\"\n    \t},\n    \t{\n      \t\"@type\": \"ListItem\",\n      \t\"position\": 2,\n      \t\"name\": \"Informative Blogs\",\n      \t\"item\": \"https://strobesnmore.com/blogs/informative\"\n    \t},\n    \t{\n      \t\"@type\": \"ListItem\",\n      \t\"position\": 3,\n      \t\"name\": \"Ohio Emergency Vehicle Light Laws\"\n    \t}\n  \t]\n\t},\n\t{\n  \t\"@type\": \"FAQPage\",\n  \t\"@id\": \"https://strobesnmore.com/blogs/informative/ohio-emergency-vehicle-light-laws#faq\",\n  \t\"mainEntity\": [\n    \t{\n      \t\"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \t\"name\": \"Do Ohio volunteer firefighters need a permit for red lights?\",\n      \t\"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \t\"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \t\"text\": \"Ohio requires certification rather than a simple permit. Under ORC § 4511.01(E)(3) a private vehicle is a public safety vehicle only when properly identified as required by the director of public safety, and the State Fire Marshal is the certifying agency. The process includes an Ohio State Highway Patrol safety inspection, a department-submitted decal application, and annual renewal.\"\n      \t}\n    \t},\n    \t{\n      \t\"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \t\"name\": \"What is the Ohio Public Safety Vehicle decal?\",\n      \t\"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \t\"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \t\"text\": \"It is a Maltese Cross decal with a date sticker, placed in the lower right-hand corner of the windshield, issued by the Division of State Fire Marshal. Inspection stickers designate the vehicle function as VF for volunteer fire fighter, VR for volunteer rescue, or both.\"\n      \t}\n    \t},\n    \t{\n      \t\"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \t\"name\": \"Can waste collection trucks use flashing lights in Ohio?\",\n      \t\"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \t\"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \t\"text\": \"Yes. A 2022 amendment to ORC § 4513.17 added stationary waste collection vehicles actively collecting garbage, refuse, trash or recyclable materials on the roadside to the list of vehicles that may display a flashing, oscillating or rotating amber light.\"\n      \t}\n    \t},\n    \t{\n      \t\"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \t\"name\": \"What does Ohio Revised Code 4513.182 cover?\",\n      \t\"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \t\"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \t\"text\": \"It governs vehicles owned, leased or hired by nursery schools, kindergartens and child care centers transporting preschool children, which must display two amber flashing lights mounted on a roof bar together with a sign reading \\\"caution, children.\\\" It is not a volunteer warning light provision.\"\n      \t}\n    \t}\n  \t]\n\t},\n\t{\n  \t\"@type\": \"Organization\",\n  \t\"@id\": \"https://strobesnmore.com/#organization\",\n  \t\"name\": \"St